# Shared review rooms

## Architecture

- `migrations/0002_teams.sql` (append-only): `teams`, `team_members` (one owner per team, enforced by a partial unique index) and `team_uploads`.
- `src/routes/teams.ts`: Hono sub-router mounted at `/api/teams`, behind the host's `requireAuth`. The existing `/api/*` same-origin check covers every mutation.
  - Every membership check reads D1 directly (no cache), so removal takes effect on the next request.
  - Team files are stored in R2 at `teams/<team>/<server-uuid>`. The D1 row must match both id and team, so another team's id returns 404 and is never deleted.
  - `src/lib/bounded.ts` holds the body reader shared with personal uploads. It counts actual bytes, so chunked bodies are bounded too.
- `src/lib/team-room.ts`: `TeamRoom`, a SQLite Durable Object per `[team, room]`. It uses `acceptWebSocket`, socket attachments (identity, lease, rate bucket) and `setWebSocketAutoResponse('ping','pong')`. There is no socket map or timer.
  - Messages are written in a transaction and pruned to the latest 50 before they are broadcast.
  - `seq` is `AUTOINCREMENT`, so it keeps increasing after pruning and restarts.
  - The DO has no public route. The only path in is the WebSocket gateway in `teams.ts`, which builds a fresh header set from the verified session and discards all client headers.
- Handshake (`GET /api/teams/:team/rooms/:room/ws`): checks session (401), membership (403), no query string, room matches `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,40}`, same-origin `Origin` (missing, `null` or foreign gives 403) and `Upgrade: websocket`.
  - The lease is `min(5 min, session expiry)`.
  - Input limits: text at most 1000 characters, frames at most 4096 UTF-8 bytes.
  - Invalid JSON or text gets an `error` event and nothing is stored. Binary and oversized frames close the socket.
- `public/teams.html`: UI with the requested `data-testid` controls. It uses the existing session cookie, renders with `textContent` only, and closes the previous socket before opening a new one.
- The `hibernating-websocket` catalog block was used as a reference only, not installed. It would have added prerelease dev dependencies, and its rate limit (10 burst, 2/s) is below the required workload. Its DO design was adapted with a 100 burst / 100 per second bucket.

## Follow-up: viewers, live revocation, retry-safe messages

- `migrations/0003_team_viewer_role.sql` (additive; 0002 is untouched): rebuilds `team_members` so the role CHECK allows `viewer`. Existing rows are copied as-is. No DO migration tag changed.
- Roles: `owner` (immutable), `member` (read/write), `viewer` (read-only). `PUT .../members/:userId` accepts `member` or `viewer`; `GET /api/teams` returns the actual role. Viewers get 403 on team upload and delete (and on membership management); download and room connect still work.
- Live revocation: the gateway also passes the verified session id, which is stored in the socket attachment. In `TeamRoom`, every application send runs one D1 query joining `sessions` and `team_members` (session not revoked or expired, member of this team). This happens before dedup lookup, conflict handling, ack or commit.
  - Removed or logged-out sender: `error` event with `code:"forbidden"`, socket closed, nothing committed.
  - Viewer sender: `error` with `code:"forbidden"`, socket stays open for receiving.
  - After the commit, each distinct recipient session is re-authorized in D1 before delivery. A recipient that fails is closed and receives nothing. Viewers still receive.
  - Re-adding a member only allows a new connection. An old socket keeps its revoked session id and stays dead.
  - Message handling is chained per DO so sends are processed in arrival order despite the D1 awaits. The dedup lookup, insert and pruning are one synchronous `transactionSync`, so simultaneous retries cannot both insert.
  - Sockets attached before this change have no session id; they are closed on their next send.
- `clientId` (optional, `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,80}`): new messages echo it in the `message` event and in snapshots. Records live in a never-pruned `dedup (userId, clientId, seq, text)` table in the room's SQLite, so retries still ack after the message leaves the 50-message window or after a restart. An exact retry sends `{type:"ack",seq,clientId}` only to the retrying socket. Different text yields `{type:"error",code:"conflict",clientId}`. Ids are scoped per user and per team/room. The `messages.clientId` column is added with `ALTER TABLE` when missing, so old rooms and legacy messages keep working.
- UI: `message-send`, `message-text` and `team-upload` are disabled for viewers once the team list loads. The role is read at load time, so a changed role needs a refresh. The server enforces it regardless. Each UI send carries a fresh `clientId`, and the page never resends after reconnect.
- Tests: `test/viewers.test.ts` covers viewer permissions, downgrade, removal, logout, re-add, ack/conflict/validation, simultaneous retries and dedup retention after pruning.

## Commands

`pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm build` (dry run), `pnpm db:local`. The tests in `test/teams.test.ts` and `test/viewers.test.ts` run the real Durable Object and WebSockets in workerd.

## Limitations

- Logout, removal and downgrade are enforced at each send and each delivery, but an idle open socket is not closed until the next fanout or send. Events already queued before the mutation response are not retracted.
- Authorization costs D1 reads per send (one for the sender, one per distinct recipient session).
- Dedup records are kept forever per room; there is no cleanup.
- A socket that is idle past its lease is closed on its next message or the next handshake.
- Only the two demo accounts can be added. Membership management is API-only, with `member` and `viewer` roles.
- The page's file list only shows files uploaded in the current page session. There is no list endpoint.
- History is bounded to 50 messages. There is no replay, exactly-once delivery or acknowledgement.
- Rate limiting is per connection and generous. It is not account or IP abuse protection.
- The browser client does not reconnect automatically. Connect again to resume.
- Platform eviction timing and billing savings are not tested or claimed.
